  "id": "COMPOUND:1515 - PROTEIN:2687",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between ursodeoxycholic acid and Cytochrome c oxidase subunit 6A2, mitochondrial, through a series of target interactions. ursodeoxycholic acid is directly linked to L132, which in turn targets cholic acid, and cholic acid targets the cytochrome c oxidase subunit 6A2. ursodeoxycholic acid is also linked to P-glycoprotein 1, which targets stigmastane-3,6-diol, and stigmastane-3,6-diol targets the same cytochrome c oxidase subunit 6A2. This suggests that ursodeoxycholic acid may act through multiple pathways to influence the activity of the cytochrome c oxidase subunit 6A2, possibly by modulating the expression or function of its targets. The evidence supports a possible role for ursodeoxycholic acid in regulating mitochondrial function through these indirect interactions, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
